Subject: main: gethostbyname() instead of gethostbyname_r() on OpenVMS

php_network_gethostbyname() calls the 6-argument gethostbyname_r() with a
malloc()ed buffer.  On OpenVMS (LP64) that buffer is above 2 GB, and
gethostbyname_r() writes through a 32-bit copy of its address: an ACCVIO
at the sign-extended address in system code.  With a _malloc32() buffer
the same call works (probe r_hostent_r).  gethostbyname() and
gethostbynamel() therefore crashed for any name that resolved (vms-php
PORTING_LOG #51).  PHP is not threaded on VMS, so it uses gethostbyname(),
whose static result needs no buffer.
---
--- a/main/network.c
+++ b/main/network.c
@@ -1408,7 +1408,11 @@
 #endif
 
 PHPAPI struct hostent*	php_network_gethostbyname(const char *name) {
-#if !defined(HAVE_GETHOSTBYNAME_R)
+#if !defined(HAVE_GETHOSTBYNAME_R) || defined(__VMS)
+	/* On OpenVMS gethostbyname_r() cannot fill a buffer above 2 GB, where
+	 * LP64 malloc() puts it: it ACCVIOs at the sign-extended 32-bit address
+	 * (vms-php PORTING_LOG #51, probe r_hostent_r).  PHP is not threaded
+	 * there, so the static result of gethostbyname() serves. */
 	return gethostbyname(name);
 #else
 	if (FG(tmp_host_buf)) {
